    "created_at": "2016-05-10T15:23:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-10T15:23:00Z",
    "body": "The current design is intentional. The input, change, and click events are explicitly for when the _user_ changes the control, not when the author changes them. (Thus, they don't fire when setting `.value` on text inputs, or similar.)\n\nIf you want to notify one part of your code when another part of your code makes changes to the control, I'd suggest firing an event---probably not one that reuses existing event names like \"click\".\n\nSince this proposal doesn't seem coherent with the existing spec's intention and doesn't propose to solve any currently-unsolvable problems, I'll close this issue. Feel free to continue discussing in the closed thread, but keep in mind https://wiki.whatwg.org/wiki/FAQ#Is_there_a_process_for_adding_new_features_to_a_specification.3F\n",
